Package: ladybird-app
Name: Ladybird
Version: @VER@
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64
Maintainer: Max Leiter <maxwell.leiter@gmail.com>
Author: Max Leiter <maxwell.leiter@gmail.com>
Depends: libicu78 (>= 78.3), libiosexec1 (>= 1.3.1)
Section: Utilities
Priority: optional
Description: Ladybird — a standalone native web browser for jailbroken iPad
 A real home-screen browser app: tap the icon, it launches standalone (no iosc /
 Wayland / desktop stack) and renders the modern web with the from-scratch Ladybird
 engine (LibWeb + LibJS, no WebKit, no JIT). The four engine services (WebContent,
 RequestServer, ImageDecoder, WebWorker) are bundled inside the .app and posix_spawn'd;
 IPC is an AF_UNIX socketpair handed over via SOCKET_TAKEOVER. Painting is presented
 zero-copy through a CAMetalLayer over the shared IOSurface backing store, with a CPU
 CoreGraphics fallback when the GPU entitlement is unavailable.
 .
 Built for iPadOS/iOS rootless (palera1n/Dopamine), /var/jb, ad-hoc + DER signed. The
 engine's Lagom libraries are statically linked into the app + helpers; only the shared
 leaf libraries (ICU 78.3, and via the engine deps the font/codec/TLS closure) come from
 /var/jb.
 .
 NOTE (provisional): the full Depends closure (harfbuzz 10, freetype, fontconfig, curl +
 openssl, sqlite3, libxml2, png/jpeg/webp, ...) is finalized against the engine agent's
 leaf deb names once the M0 engine build lands. libskia is static (no dep).
